cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use redherring or its study of red herrings in open-source CI, please cite it."
title: "redherring: find the CI failures that weren't your fault"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool and GitHub Action that mines GitHub Actions history for runs that failed and then
  passed on a re-run of the same commit, naming the flaky tests and infrastructure causes. Includes a
  study of 122 popular repositories (1.25 million workflow runs over 14 days).
type: software
authors:
  - alias: ixklo
repository-code: "https://github.com/ixklo/redherring"
url: "https://github.com/ixklo/redherring"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.1
date-released: 2026-09-28
keywords:
  - flaky tests
  - continuous integration
  - GitHub Actions
  - software testing
